<!-- ============ PROBLEM + REAL PROBLEM — combined ============ -->
<section id="problem" class="real bg-grid bg-grid-dark">
  <div class="wrap real-grid">
    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="sec-label">The problem</div>
      <h2>Your clinical work is not the bottleneck. <em>Patient admin</em> is.</h2>
      <p>You already know how to diagnose, treat and care. What slows you down is everything around it: chasing intake forms, reviewing lab results, drafting referrals, evidencing safeguarding, coordinating recalls and chasing missing information.</p>
      <div class="problem-cards">
        <div class="pcard">
          <span class="pcard-k">01 / Records</span>
          <h4>Patient intake</h4>
          <p>Forms, history, allergies, consents, screening.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pcard pcard-dark">
          <span class="pcard-k">02 / Risk</span>
          <h4>Medication &amp; interactions</h4>
          <p>Drug-drug, allergies, dosing, contraindications.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pcard">
          <span class="pcard-k">03 / Evidence</span>
          <h4>Notes &amp; referrals</h4>
          <p>SOAP notes, referral letters, lab follow-ups.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pcard pcard-lime">
          <span class="pcard-k">04 / Patient work</span>
          <h4>Patient chase</h4>
          <p>Draft SMS, emails, and follow-up questions.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="real-col">
      <div class="transcript reveal reveal-delay-2">
        <div class="sec-label">The real problem</div>

        <div class="transcript-stage">
          <img class="transcript-photo" src="/images/the-real-problem.png" alt="An exhausted GP at a desk surrounded by patient notes" />

          <div class="stage-overlay">
            <div class="stage-quote-wrap">
              <blockquote class="stage-quote">
                I feel like I'm working at <span class="hl">full capacity</span>, but I can't grow the practice because admin eats my time.
              </blockquote>
              <div class="sig stage-sig">— GP using Mia Clinic Admin</div>
            </div>

            <div class="notes-wall" aria-hidden="true">
              <div class="note note-1">
                <span class="note-tape"></span>
                <p>"Lab returned Friday. Recall went out Wednesday. Patient noticed."</p>
                <span class="note-attr">— GP, Birmingham</span>
              </div>
              <div class="note note-2 note-lime">
                <span class="note-tape"></span>
                <p>"Recall list is 11 conditions. Miss one, missed diagnosis."</p>
                <span class="note-attr">— Practice manager, Bristol</span>
              </div>
              <div class="note note-3">
                <span class="note-tape"></span>
                <p>"Notes at 11pm. My family sees me less than my EMIS."</p>
                <span class="note-attr">— GP partner, Manchester</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="body-txt">
          The admin around each patient sets the cap. <strong>More patients means more intake forms to chase</strong>, more lab results to review, more referrals to write, more recalls to track. So the team either stops growing the list, or takes it on and pays for it with evenings and weekends.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

