        <div class="qa-body"><p>No. You remain the clinician. It checks the record, evidence, notes and gaps before the consult. You make every decision.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="qa reveal reveal-delay-2">
        <div class="qa-head">
          <span class="qn">Q2</span>
          <h4>Will this work with my EMIS, SystmOne or Vision?</h4>
          <span class="qa-tog">+</span>
        </div>
        <div class="qa-body"><p>Yes. Use it as a pre-check before your normal consult, prescribing or referral process. It fits around what you already do.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="qa reveal reveal-delay-3">
        <div class="qa-head">
          <span class="qn">Q3</span>
          <h4>What about patient data?</h4>
          <span class="qa-tog">+</span>
        </div>
        <div class="qa-body"><p>Data is handled under your clinic-approved process. Add your privacy and clinical governance wording here. We walk through the exact data handling on the call.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="qa reveal reveal-delay-2">
        <div class="qa-head">
          <span class="qn">Q4</span>
          <h4>What if the patient still asks a question?</h4>
          <span class="qa-tog">+</span>
        </div>
        <div class="qa-body"><p>Some queries cannot be avoided. But reviewed records reduce the avoidable ones: the missed recall, the unflagged interaction, the unfiled consent.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="qa reveal reveal-delay-3">
        <div class="qa-head">
          <span class="qn">Q5</span>
          <h4>Can it draft SMS and email messages?</h4>
          <span class="qa-tog">+</span>
        </div>
        <div class="qa-body"><p>Yes. Patient chases, follow-up questions, and response wording, all drafted from the actual record. You review before sending.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="qa reveal reveal-delay-4">
        <div class="qa-head">
          <span class="qn">Q6</span>
          <h4>What happens on the demo call?</h4>
          <span class="qa-tog">+</span>
        </div>
        <div class="qa-body"><p>Bring one live patient or a typical week. We review it together in about 20 minutes. You see the flags, the drafted messages, and the missing items. Then you decide if it is worth continuing.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

